This Helm chart deploys OVN-Kubernetes, an OVN-based CNI plugin for Kubernetes that provides network virtualization, network policy, services, and overlay networking for pods.

For installation instructions, see:

- [Launching OVN-Kubernetes with Helm](../../docs/installation/launching-ovn-kubernetes-with-helm.md) — Kind quickstart and step-by-step install.
- [Launching OVN-Kubernetes with kubeadm](../../docs/installation/INSTALL.KUBEADM.md) — multi-VM walkthrough on a `kubeadm`-bootstrapped cluster.

The rest of this README documents the chart values.
{{ template "chart.valuesSectionHtml" . }}

### Multiple kubelet cgroups

Set `global.kubeletCgroupPaths` to a list of cgroup v2 paths relative to
`/sys/fs/cgroup`, for example:

```yaml
global:
  kubeletCgroupPaths:
    - kubelet.slice/kubelet.service
    - podruntime/kubelet
```

A non-empty list overrides `global.kubeletCgroupPath`; an empty list preserves
single-path configuration or automatic discovery. Every process in these cgroups
can reach primary UDN pods. All paths must exist on each node. See the
[UDN host isolation documentation](../../docs/features/user-defined-networks/user-defined-networks.md)
for validation and restart behavior.
